      "markdown_value_template": "easy-blank-positive-quadratic",
      "specific_description": "Negative numerator -16t; positive quadratic 2t\u00b2+3; blank expects -4 ln(2t\u00b2+3), omits printed +K; real domain all t.",
      "original_parameters": {
        "k": -16,
        "a": 2,
        "b": 0,
        "c": 3,
        "n": 2,
        "variable": "t"
      },
      "original_prompt": "$\\int \\frac{-16t}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t=\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,K.$",
      "original_solution": "Let $u=2{t}^{2}+3.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=4t\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can solve the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-16t}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}t & =-16\\int \\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}+3}\\cdot t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-16\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+K \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2{t}^{2}+3)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "field_type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
      "field_key": "field-1",
      "bank_profile": null,
      "choices": [
